We are looking for a Senior IT Security Engineer specializing in Incident Response to serve as the primary liaison between Americas IT Operations teams and the global Cyber Defense Center.
The role coordinates the full security incident lifecycle across the region, combining global response standards with local operational context. The engineer will lead incident triage, containment, recovery, forensic analysis, stakeholder communication, and continuous improvement while strengthening regional readiness for traditional and AI-enabled cyber threats.
Key Responsibilities:

• Serve as the primary point of contact between Americas IT Operations teams and the global Cyber Defense Center for security incident management activities;

• Coordinate incident triage, containment, eradication, recovery, escalation, and post-incident review for events affecting Americas IT assets;

• Manage the regional incident lifecycle from detection through closure, ensuring alignment with global processes and addressing regional operational gaps;

• Maintain timely, clear, and consistent communication with technical teams, regional stakeholders, senior management, and executive audiences;

• Develop a detailed understanding of regional organizations, business units, technology environments, operational workflows, risks, and dependencies;

• Handle digital evidence in a forensically sound manner, preserving chain of custody, integrity, and documentation standards;

• Perform security analysis and digital forensics across Windows, Linux or UNIX, cloud, network, email, endpoint, and enterprise environments;

• Analyze alerts, logs, threat intelligence, tickets, and reports from multiple sources, including SIEM and security operations platforms;

• Prepare investigation findings, incident briefings, risk assessments, and post-incident reports for technical and non-technical audiences;

• Monitor AI-enabled attack techniques and defensive capabilities, including deepfakes, automated phishing, adversarial machine learning, response automation, and AI-assisted threat intelligence;

• Contribute to incident response playbooks, runbooks, standard operating procedures, tooling, and service improvement initiatives;

• Mentor junior incident responders and share expertise across the regional security organization.

