• Strong expertise in cybersecurity incident response, security operations, incident coordination, containment, recovery, and post-incident analysis;

• Hands-on knowledge of digital forensics, evidence handling, chain of custody, log analysis, threat intelligence, and investigative documentation;

• Experience with SIEM platforms, security monitoring tools, email and ticketing systems, and enterprise security operations workflows;

• Broad knowledge of enterprise technologies, including Windows, Linux or UNIX, directory services, AWS, Azure, mobile device management, virtualization, networks, web servers, databases, and firewalls;

• Proficiency in at least one programming or scripting language, such as Python, PowerShell, or Bash;

• Understanding of security control development, security operations, security risk management, and enterprise security governance;

• Familiarity with AI and machine learning concepts as they relate to cybersecurity threats, detection, response automation, and defensive technologies;

• Strong analytical thinking, problem-solving, prioritization, and decision-making skills during high-impact incidents;

